प्रेक्षिन्, ई, इणी, इ, looking at, viewing, regarding;
watching narrowly, scrutinizing [cf. मुख-प्˚];
having the eyes or glance of [cf. मृग-प्˚, वृक-प्˚];
जिह्म-प्रेक्षिन्, looking aside, looking askance.
—प्रेक्षि-त्व, अम्, n. the act of watching nar-
rowly, scrutinizing.

प्रेङ्खत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, shaking, moving, oscil-
lating, vibrating; wandering (?); diffusing (?);
touching (?).

प्रेप्सु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to attain, desirous of
obtaining, wishing, seeking, longing for (with acc.);
aiming at, having in view; supposing, assuming;
anxious to rescue or save; तत्-प्रेप्सु, उस्, m. (in
Ved. gram.) epithet of a particular form of the
Desiderative.

प्रेरित, अस्, आ, अम्, driven forwards, impelled,
influenced, instigated; excited, urged, stimulated;
incited to speak; sent, directed, dispatched; ordered;
touched; (अस्), m. an envoy, a messenger.

प्रेषित, अस्, आ, अम्, sent forth, sent away; sent
into exile, banished; sent, dispatched (on an errand);
ordered, directed; turned, directed (as the eyes).
